---
import SubPageLayout from '../layouts/SubPageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { isRealUrl } from '../lib/content';
---
<SubPageLayout title="Colophon" description="How Will Perry Evans built this site.">
  <article class="colophon">
    <h1>How I built this site</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I built this site myself with Claude Code, an AI coding assistant, over about a week in
        November 2026. I wrote the content and made the design decisions, and I used Claude Code to
        write and test the code. I reviewed every change before it went live. The site is built with
        Astro and hosted on GitHub Pages, and the full source is public on GitHub
        {
          isRealUrl(site.repoUrl) ? (
            <>
              {' '}at{' '}
              <a class="inline-link" href={site.repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                {site.repoUrl}
              </a>.
            </>
          ) : (
            <>.</>
          )
        }
      </p>
      <p>
        I wanted to build it this way partly because I think people who lead technology in public
        service should have their hands on the tools. Using an AI assistant well takes the same
        habits as supervising any new team member. You need to be clear about the goal, check the
        work, and stay responsible for what ships.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SubPageLayout>

<style>
  .colophon h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
</style>
